🚀 Project 3: Sentiment Analysis | Machine Learning

Excited to share my Project 3 – Sentiment Analysis

In this project, I built a Multiclass Sentiment Analysis model to classify text into four categories:
🔴 Negative
🟢 Positive
🔵 Neutral
⚪ Irrelevant

🔍 What I worked on:
• Text preprocessing and cleaning
• Converting text into numerical features using TF-IDF (Term Frequency–
Inverse Document Frequency)
• Train-Test Split
• Building a Multinomial Naive Bayes classification model
• Model prediction and evaluation
• Accuracy, Classification Report & Confusion Matrix
• Testing the model on new/unseen comments

🛠️ Technologies & Libraries:
🐍 Python
📊 Pandas & NumPy
🤖 Scikit-learn
📝 NLP / Text Preprocessing
📈 TF-IDF
🧠 Multinomial Naive Bayes
📊 Matplotlib & Seaborn

This project helped me strengthen my understanding of Natural Language Processing (NLP), text feature engineering, multiclass classification, and model evaluation.
